Tofu project-bar pet — provenance & license
============================================

These PNG frames (oneko-*.png) are the art for the chibi CAT that roams the
project bar (see static/js/tofu-pet.js). The 18 poses are:
idle / happy / sleepy / sleeping / thinking / surprised / sad / celebrating /
alert / walk1-4 / groom1-3 / scratch1-2.

Current art: AI-GENERATED original character (2026-07, refined pixel-art)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
The frames shipped here are an ORIGINAL "refined chibi pixel-art kitten"
character (a cream/sage-green/caramel calico with a green leaf-flower bandana
and a gold bell), produced by AI image generation and post-processed in this
repo. They are NOT the oneko/Neko sprite art. The directory name `oneko/` and
the `oneko-` filename prefix are retained only as the stable path the pet FSM
resolves (`_frameUrl`); they no longer denote oneko provenance.

This is the 2026-07-10 art refresh: the earlier soft-vector calico was replaced
in place (owner: "pet designs too simple; want a more refined, better-looking
set") by a richer pixel-art rendering. The approved base idle is
_candidates/cand-pixel-idle.png; the 18 poses (px-*.png) are edit-chained off
it and normalized by debug/pet_frame_pipeline.py.

How these frames were produced
------------------------------
1. One approved idle pose was generated, then every other pose was generated as
   an EDIT of that single idle (image-to-image, source_image=idle) so the
   character — fur markings, leaf bandana, proportions, palette — stays locked
   across all 18 frames. Side/walk poses were chained off a known-good side
   frame; groom2/3 off groom1; scratch2 off scratch1.
2. The raw generations came back as opaque RGB (baked checker/white bg). A
   border-connected, low-chroma flood fill (debug/pet_frame_pipeline.py) cut a
   true alpha channel — the cat's continuous chromatic outline stops the fill,
   so the cream interior is preserved — with a 1px edge feather.
3. Frames were size-normalized on BODY PIXEL AREA (not raw height, so curled
   nap/groom poses don't balloon) and anchored on the body centroid-x + bottom
   baseline (so the pet doesn't jitter or slide between poses), then downscaled
   to 128x128 RGBA.

License
-------
AI-generated imagery of this kind is treated by this project as original
project art, redistributable in every export mode (personal / internal /
opensource). These are normal committed source assets — NOT `.tofu*` agent
artifacts. There is no third-party copyright or attribution requirement carried
by these files.

Historical note
---------------
Earlier revisions of this directory shipped per-pose slices of the classic
public-domain "Neko" sprite sheet (oneko.gif, from https://github.com/adryd325/
oneko.js — code MIT (c) 2022 adryd; the 1989 Neko art is public domain). Those
slices have been REPLACED by the generated character above and are no longer
present. The originals are retained out-of-tree (repo-root .icon-backups/,
gitignored) for reference only.
